# Runtime modules whose emit-jvm output the JVM verifier rejects, known and owned:
# project<TAB>why. Classified by the verifier reason on 55698b009 (conformance lane, 2026-09-28);
# (A)-(E) are the causes jvm-verifies.ts names; its run prints the live counts, so none are kept
# here to go stale. A module that verifies again prints "remove it".
#
# **A module count barely moves when a cause is fixed, and that is not the fix failing.** The
# verifier stops at a class's first error, so it answers *whether* a module loads, never *how many*
# causes stand behind that. On 2026-09-29 (B) and (D) were fixed and failing modules went 19 -> 18:
# url verifies whole, and net, stream and zlib now stop at the error that (B) had masked -- stream
# at (A), net at (E) PerformanceNodeEntry, zlib at (E) Transform. (B) was the first failure in
# those three only, not nine as first classified.
# (A) was fixed the same day and the count stayed 18: seven modules lost (A), and five of them
# now stop at (G), an async frame emit-jvm declines under NTS4013, while fs and stream stop at (E).
# (G) was fixed next and the count stayed 18 again: those five now stop at (E), a closure declined
# at another generic instantiation -- the closure-slot family, which lowering owns, not the backend.
# (F) next: child_process and cluster lose their only INVALID and stop at (E), classes never written.
# Then the fewer-parameter bridges: zlib 28 missing -> 1, crypto 11 -> 1, stream and fs 5 -> 1, http 12
# missing -> 1 INVALID; four now stop at (H), a duplicate member, and http at (I).
# (H) was one function in two dispatch slots, written as two methods of one name and descriptor;
# those four now stop at the closure-slot family. **(H) is unguarded too**: no reduction reproduced
# the two slots (two instantiations of AsyncIterable, most likely), so stream is its only witness,
# and a MISSING is not something a pin can hold.
# (I): a closure call's arguments were loaded unchecked; they are now checked as a direct call's,
# so http's Socket-for-HTTPDuplex is a named decline rather than a VerifyError in Program.
# (C) and most of the closure-slot declines: one abstract root every callable class extends
# (`types::callable_class`) -- 81 closure-store declines -> 32, and readline verifies whole.
#
# **(B) is an unguarded fix.** Its only witness is the runtime: every reduction gave the value a
# layout and verified before the fix, so no fixture holds it, and while stream and net fail for
# other reasons a regression of (B) prints "known" like everything else. (D) has a unit test,
# body.rs `a_number_converted_to_a_bool_puts_a_label_between_a_definition_and_its_read`.
runtime/node/dns	(E) a class the JVM declines under NTS4009 (an override at another representation), referenced and never written (classified, 2026-09-28)
runtime/node/child_process	(E) ChildWritable, referenced and never written -- lowering refuses its `_write`, an override narrowing an erased chunk (live on C, a-writable-override-narrowing-an-erased-chunk), and Program references a ClosureN beside it; the first failure since (F) cleared (jvm lane, 2026-09-29)
runtime/node/cluster	(E) ChildWritable, as child_process's, and PerformanceNodeEntry, the perf_hooks family, both referenced and never written -- the first failure since (F) cleared (jvm lane, 2026-09-29)
runtime/node/dgram	(E) PerformanceNodeEntry, referenced by Program and never written -- the perf_hooks family; (B) was not live here on 41dd45663 (jvm lane, 2026-09-29)
runtime/node/net	(E) PerformanceNodeEntry, referenced by Program and never written -- the perf_hooks family; the first failure since (B) cleared, jvm lane, 2026-09-29
runtime/node/http	(E) PerformanceNodeEntry, the perf_hooks family (a covariant record return), referenced by Program and never written -- the first failure since (I) became a named decline: a Socket where HTTPDuplex is declared, which C gets wrong where the fields are reordered (jvm lane, 2026-09-29)
runtime/node/process	(E) a class the JVM declines under NTS4009 (an override at another representation), referenced and never written (classified, 2026-09-28) -- (B) was not the first failure here on 41dd45663 (jvm lane, 2026-09-29)
tooling/conformance/outcomes/a-closure-passed-to-an-interface-method-through-a-field	(C) the witness for it: a closure class that does not implement the callback's signature at an invokeinterface reached through a field (conformance lane, 2026-09-28)
runtime/node/perf_hooks	(E) classes the JVM declines under NTS4009 (overrides at another representation), referenced and never written: PerformanceNodeTiming, PerformanceNodeEntry, PerformanceResourceTiming -- the family build-floor already blocks, classes only a return or a subclass reaches (classified; owner confirmed, 2026-09-28)
tooling/conformance/outcomes/a-controller-stored-by-a-generic-branch	(E) the witness for it: the JVM declines the closure under NTS4009 at another instantiation; C agrees (conformance lane, 2026-09-28)
